main/iwd: pin the D-Bus data directory so cross builds are correct.

iwd's configure resolves the dbus-1 datadir via
`$PKG_CONFIG --variable=datadir dbus-1` (configure.ac:216) when
--with-dbus-datadir is not given. Under cbuild's cross environment
pkgconf answers with the SYSROOT-prefixed path, so the D-Bus policy and
activation files are packaged under
usr/<triplet>/usr/share/dbus-1/{system.d,system-services}/ instead of
usr/share/dbus-1/. On the image dbus-daemon then has no policy allowing
root to own net.connman.iwd, RequestName is denied, and iwd crash-loops
with "Name request failed / D-Bus disconnected, quitting..." (observed
live on the Astro qemu-armv7 image; the armv7 repo is self-built so
main/iwd is cross-compiled — Chimera's native builders never hit this).
Pass the real path explicitly; native builds get the identical result
they already had. pkgrel bumped so the broken r0 armv7 apk is superseded.

diff --git a/main/iwd/template.py b/main/iwd/template.py
--- a/main/iwd/template.py
+++ b/main/iwd/template.py
@@ -1,12 +1,15 @@
 pkgname = "iwd"
 pkgver = "3.12"
-pkgrel = 0
+pkgrel = 1
 build_style = "gnu_configure"
 configure_args = [
     # junk cflags that redefine FORTIFY
     "--disable-optimization",
     "--disable-systemd-service",
     "--enable-dbus-policy",
+    # explicit: the default is `pkgconf --variable=datadir dbus-1`, which
+    # is sysroot-prefixed in cross builds and mispackages the policy files
+    "--with-dbus-datadir=/usr/share",
     "--enable-wired",
     "--enable-pie",
 ]
